I wrote two task files and the issue responses to session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The plan's || true covers that case, so the files are on disk where the next phase reads them, and I didn't force-add them.

Task 1: #977 layer 3 (product, outside `dispatch`). sub_agent and explore_agent children get their own bash, and when the parent is a spawn worker pinned to one directory, that bash should block the same git redirection tricks the parent blocks (--git-dir, -C, GIT_DIR=). The rule is that no bash a child can run is looser than its parent's. The parent's check is at src/tools.rs:354, and the comment at :1589 says the child skips it.
• **Step 1 checks whether this can happen at all:** can a pinned parent ever create a child? If not, the task pins that with a test and fixes the comment instead of building plumbing nothing uses.
• **If it can:** the parent's directory gets passed down to the child, which then uses the parent's own check and refusal message.
• **Tests:** blocked cases, allowed cases (including an unpinned child, which is every ordinary session), a check that each blocked input really trips the detector, and a break-it-then-restore control.

Task 2: #982 slice (product). yoyo docs <missing crate> will exit 1, and yoyo config get <typo> will exit 2, the same code yoyo model <bad> uses. A real key that just isn't set still exits 0, and that case is the regression check. Both commands already make the right call since this morning's session; only the exit code is missing.
• I put this in the second slot because it's filed issue work. Every self-driven pick avoids dispatch, which took 4 of the last 8 changes.
• Before wiring the exit, the task checks for tests that call these commands in-process, because a call that exits would kill the whole test binary.
• The #982 comment has to state how many failure paths still exit 0 before describing this fix. #982 stays open.

